{"lines":[{"w":0.060194174448649079,"x":0.093203882994122078,"h":0.015988371899566145,"y":0.043604651059664601,"t":"Test 2","c":1},{"h":0.017464500498548863,"c":1,"x":0.093203880819928836,"w":0.30873786926269531,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","y":0.091569767324853557},{"x":0.093138499878357567,"y":0.13061213480114364,"w":0.82343739827473961,"c":1,"h":0.02196874648239755,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading"},{"y":0.15109034260457332,"x":0.091262138043737617,"w":0.17087378184000651,"t":"Passage 3 below.","h":0.019003115264797477,"c":1},{"x":0.42096600579355825,"w":0.17573384602864583,"t":"An ideal city","y":0.18784794538320071,"h":0.024625967150536554,"c":1},{"y":0.23367238494181897,"t":"Leonardo da Vinci's ideal city was centuries ahead of its time","c":1,"h":0.021553284356898628,"w":0.61955657958984378,"x":0.19799006252688212},{"h":0.019003115264797366,"c":1,"w":0.74368932088216144,"y":0.27320872291811016,"t":"The word 'genius' is universally associated with the name of Leonardo da Vinci. A true","x":0.091262135584423726},{"x":0.091147497017847842,"w":0.75165985107421873,"y":0.28989788687644658,"c":1,"h":0.021905926380573315,"t":"Renaissance man, he embodied scientific spirit, artistic talent and humanist sensibilities."},{"t":"Five hundred years have passed since Leonardo died in his home at Château du Clos Lucé,","y":0.30959302334322769,"w":0.77475728352864581,"x":0.091262142332764334,"h":0.018895348284474811,"c":1},{"x":0.091171461692389447,"y":0.32747524758960544,"t":"outside Tours, France. Yet far from fading into insignificance, his thinking has carried down the","w":0.81376993815104159,"c":1,"h":0.02180907704005719},{"h":0.020429802535107511,"t":"centuries and still surprises today.","w":0.28978790283203126,"c":1,"x":0.091067591051321464,"y":0.34601475347658583},{"t":"The Renaissance marked the transition from the 15th century to modernity and took place after","h":0.019748453633436136,"c":1,"x":0.091196111867428625,"y":0.38362685004084529,"w":0.81178614298502616},{"h":0.020222266366548558,"x":0.09119610696966958,"t":"the spread of the plague in the 14th century, which caused a global crisis resulting in some","w":0.77100290934244786,"c":1,"y":0.40240380764281269},{"c":1,"x":0.091262143910487148,"y":0.42149532717881777,"w":0.80194173177083339,"t":"200 million deaths across Europe and Asia. Today, the world is on the cusp of a climate crisis,","h":0.019003115264797588},{"h":0.020580477135203723,"x":0.091204050663631145,"y":0.43986140159614928,"w":0.81758168538411446,"t":"which is predicted to cause widespread displacement, extinctions and death, if left unaddressed.","c":1},{"w":0.7535527038574219,"y":0.45847517449656827,"h":0.021335395028658,"x":0.091198805955219106,"c":1,"t":"Then, as now, radical solutions were called for to revolutionise the way people lived and"},{"c":1,"x":0.091262130763670277,"t":"safeguard humanity against catastrophe.","w":0.34563107808430987,"h":0.017545098753361743,"y":0.47965116267463115},{"c":1,"t":"Around 1486 - after a pestilence that killed half the population in Milan, Italy - Leonardo turned","x":0.091200750014284612,"h":0.02095213084948766,"w":0.82731348673502603,"y":0.51415189627230518},{"t":"his thoughts to urban planning problems. Following a typical Renaissance trend, he began to","w":0.79029123942057278,"c":1,"h":0.019003115264797477,"y":0.53333333357331603,"x":0.091262147365405805},{"h":0.020560747663551426,"w":0.82718444824218762,"t":"work on an 'ideal city' project, which - due to its excessive costs - would remain unfulfilled. Yet","x":0.09126214472185315,"y":0.55077881660993788,"c":1},{"h":0.019585016434809144,"t":"given that unsustainable urban models are a key cause of global climate change today, it's only","y":0.57055463245625282,"x":0.091202977805011562,"w":0.80980916341145837,"c":1},{"h":0.019366571539287558,"c":1,"w":0.69332107543945309,"t":"natural to wonder how Leonardo might have changed the shape of modern cities.","x":0.091195253628387526,"y":0.58972355815374422},{"x":0.093203883428949627,"y":0.62790697663033579,"t":"Although the Renaissance is renowned as an era of incredible progress in art and architecture,","h":0.017575889658705046,"w":0.80000000000000004,"c":1},{"x":0.091170418111452142,"w":0.77881581624348961,"h":0.020769293954439272,"c":1,"t":"it is rarely noted that the 15th century also marked the birth of urbanism as a true academic","y":0.64381136198394484},{"h":0.019875079003449869,"w":0.79428716023763024,"y":0.66364053512234877,"t":"discipline. The rigour and method behind the conscious conception of a city had been largely","x":0.091211641974480048,"c":1},{"w":0.81954416910807304,"t":"missing in Western thought until the moment when prominent Renaissance men pushed forward","c":1,"x":0.091207853160684166,"y":0.68289652529667189,"h":0.019326302121361438},{"c":1,"x":0.091170578414329295,"y":0.70067482992163432,"w":0.78076426188151049,"h":0.021421144907348255,"t":"large-scale urban projects in Italy, such as the reconfiguration of the town of Pienza and the"},{"t":"expansion of the city of Ferrara. These works surely inspired Leonardo's decision to rethink the","x":0.093081622622901442,"h":0.02261156694168609,"y":0.71834537905983709,"w":0.81383677164713542,"c":1},{"w":0.78280563354492194,"t":"design of medieval cities, with their winding and overcrowded streets and with houses piled","y":0.73585007853247208,"h":0.024088836384710821,"x":0.093078224225186634,"c":1},{"x":0.094950704732371438,"t":"against one another.","c":1,"w":0.17116886138916015,"y":0.75881551946677628,"h":0.016079619220484065},{"h":0.019111469304450179,"x":0.091197766092862856,"t":"It is not easy to identify a coordinated vision of Leonardo's ideal city because of his disordered","y":0.79400708064363412,"c":1,"w":0.81180094401041658},{"w":0.80210530598958341,"t":"way of working with notes and sketches. But from the largest collection of Leonardo's papers","c":1,"h":0.020388839103722578,"x":0.093120450391091084,"y":0.8122120806292531},{"x":0.093147614324857769,"y":0.83125049957130692,"w":0.82342997233072923,"t":"ever assembled, a series of innovative thoughts can be reconstructed regarding the foundation of","h":0.01997211254274367,"c":1},{"x":0.093092749441711545,"h":0.021197875786421738,"t":"a new city along the Ticino River, which runs from Switzerland into Italy and is 248 kilometres","y":0.84955472957132527,"c":1,"w":0.81380905151367189},{"h":0.020647253351419481,"c":1,"y":0.86898707099221073,"x":0.0912106920303042,"t":"long. He designed the city for the easy transport of goods and clean urban spaces, and he wanted","w":0.82536249796549477},{"h":0.018895348284474811,"x":0.093203885170123804,"c":1,"t":"a comfortable and spacious city, with well-ordered streets and architecture. He recommended","y":0.88808139562185429,"w":0.79417475382486979},{"w":0.74951456705729169,"c":1,"t":"'high, strong walls', with 'towers and battlements of all necessary and pleasant beauty'.","y":0.90685358241295333,"x":0.093203881447646686,"h":0.020560747663551315},{"h":0.015988371899566145,"c":1,"w":0.027184467315673838,"x":0.093203882742461816,"t":"48","y":0.95930232561663009}],"w":2400,"h":3209}